.TH MU2EDAQ-TOOLS-INFO 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-tools\-info \- report the config file the C++ library would choose
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-tools\-info
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-tools\-info
.BR \-V | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the version compiled into
.B mu2edaq_cli_core
and the result of
.BR mu2edaq::cli::find_config ()
from the current directory.
It reads no YAML and no settings; the C++ library has no YAML parser.
.PP
It is the counterpart to
.BR "mu2edaq\-tools config" ,
but the two search lists differ, so the files they report can differ from the
same directory; see FILES.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are processed left to right;
.B \-h
and
.B \-V
exit as soon as they are seen.
Only the separate-argument form
.B \-c
.I FILE
is accepted, not
.BR \-\-config=FILE .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Make
.I FILE
the only candidate.
No
.B ~
expansion is done.
A
.I FILE
that does not exist prints
.B (none found, using defaults)
and exits 0.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-paths
Also list every candidate in search order, marking the chosen one with
.BR * .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print
.B mu2edaq\-tools\-info
.I version
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
The first existing regular file in:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG        (used literally, no ~ expansion)
\&./mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
\&./config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml
$HOME/.config/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml
/etc/mu2edaq/commandline\-tools.yaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
On Windows
.B USERPROFILE
(else
.BR HOMEDRIVE HOMEPATH )
replaces
.BR HOME .
The Python list has one more entry between the third and fourth lines of
this list, the package's own
.IR config/mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.yaml ,
which for the editable install always exists.
From any directory without its own config file, the Python tools then read
the checkout's file while this tool reports the user or system file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
First candidate when
.B \-c
is absent.
.TP
.B HOME
Base of the user candidate.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including when no file is found.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown option, or
.B \-c
without an argument.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools\-info \-\-paths
MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG=$HOME/site.yaml mu2edaq\-tools\-info
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq_cli_core (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
